  "new_findings": [
    "Same motif changes thickness, activity and articulation; preserving recognisable group shapes is not replacing differing notes with simile.",
    "Long upper holds, inner syncopated chords and receiving ties need separate reading roles; no universal split-every-beat or flatten-beams instruction.",
    "Beam groups and longer slurs serve different scales. Three/four-bar systems and a final six-bar system are judged by content, not a fixed bar-count template.",
    "Densest activity changes between hands and by beat; no A047 interval measurement or minimum-space proof was performed.",
    "Known D.S./Coda route has visible landing clarity but real cross-page search costs; printed p239/240 recommendations are not all followed literally.",
